<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<WorkflowBuilder Version="2.9.0"
                 xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
                 xmlns:rx="clr-namespace:Bonsai.Reactive;assembly=Bonsai.Core"
                 xmlns:sys="clr-namespace:System;assembly=mscorlib"
                 xmlns:scr="clr-namespace:Bonsai.Scripting.Expressions;assembly=Bonsai.Scripting.Expressions"
                 xmlns:harp="clr-namespace:Bonsai.Harp;assembly=Bonsai.Harp"
                 xmlns:core="clr-namespace:OpenRigs.Core;assembly=OpenRigs.Core"
                 xmlns:dev="clr-namespace:OpenRigs.Devices;assembly=OpenRigs.Devices"
                 xmlns:zap="clr-namespace:OpenRigs.Devices.Zapit;assembly=OpenRigs.Devices"
                 xmlns:orcl="clr-namespace:OpenRigs.Control;assembly=OpenRigs.Control"
                 xmlns:orl="clr-namespace:OpenRigs.Logging;assembly=OpenRigs.Logging"
                 xmlns:hd="clr-namespace:OpenRigs.HarpDevices;assembly=OpenRigs.HarpDevices"
                 xmlns:mf="clr-namespace:OpenRigs.Manifest;assembly=OpenRigs.Manifest"
                 xmlns:lv="clr-namespace:OpenRigs.LiveView;assembly=OpenRigs.LiveView"
                 xmlns:gl="clr-namespace:Bonsai.Shaders;assembly=Bonsai.Shaders"
                 xmlns:al="clr-namespace:Bonsai.Audio;assembly=Bonsai.Audio"
                 xmlns:dsp="clr-namespace:Bonsai.Dsp;assembly=Bonsai.Dsp"
                 xmlns:aud="clr-namespace:OpenRigs.Audio;assembly=OpenRigs.Audio"
                 xmlns:p1="clr-namespace:;assembly=Extensions"
                 xmlns:p2="clr-namespace:OpenRigs.Devices.Rigs;assembly=OpenRigs.Devices"
                 xmlns:p6="clr-namespace:UclOpenCoenDomeDecisionMakingTask;assembly=Extensions"
                 xmlns="https://bonsai-rx.org/2018/workflow">
  <Workflow>
    <Nodes>
      <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
        <Name>RigSetup</Name>
        <Description>Reads this machine's rig.yml (ConfigRoot\MachineName\rig.yml, ReadRigConfig) into RigConfigs, the lab rig model (open_rigs.rigs.lab_rig.LabRig, generated C#), and publishes RigConfigDirectory. Everything else takes its devices and calibrations from these two.</Description>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
              <Name>ReadRigConfig</Name>
              <Description>Resolves this machine's rig configuration directory (ConfigRoot\MachineName), publishes it as RigConfigDirectory, and reads rig.yml from it. Fails at startup if either is missing.</Description>
              <Workflow>
                <Nodes>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="core:ResolveRigConfigDirectory">
                      <core:ConfigRoot>C:\Coen-Lab-Local\RigConfigs</core:ConfigRoot>
                    </Combinator>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="rx:AsyncSubject">
                    <Name>RigConfigDirectory</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Core:ReadRigConfig.bonsai">
                    <FileName>rig.yml</FileName>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowOutput" />
                </Nodes>
                <Edges>
                  <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="2" To="3" Label="Source1" />
                </Edges>
              </Workflow>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="p2:DeserializeFromYaml">
              <p2:Type xsi:type="TypeMapping" TypeArguments="p2:LabRig" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Take">
                <rx:Count>1</rx:Count>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:AsyncSubject">
              <Name>RigConfigs</Name>
            </Expression>
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="2" To="3" Label="Source1" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
        <Property Name="SubjectId" />
        <Property Name="SessionId" />
        <Property Name="TaskPath" />
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
        <Name>Initialization</Name>
        <Description>The experiment controller (OpenRigs.Control, ExperimentControl) over TCP 5561: SubjectId (the mouse's lab ID, or test) and SessionId are the launch's; the parameters a controller may change until Go (TrainingStage, SpoutStepSize; the task's own settings are the task file's, which rig-control writes at launch and again at Go with the form's edits, and names in TaskPath) and the commands it may send while ready or recording. The workflow starts into ready mode (devices connected, spouts homed and at this mouse's positions, live view on, nothing recorded) and reports Ready from Hardware. TaskFilePath (TaskPath) is published at Start; Go publishes RunSettings (SubjectId, SessionId, TrainingStage). SpoutStepSize follows the controller live, its one default its subject's, shown to the controller by ParameterDefault a second after Start. ManualRewardDropUl is the 2.5 ul every RewardLeft and RewardRight gives before and during a run through the valve's calibration (Pip's fixed manual drop, 15 Nov 2026).</Description>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
              <Property Name="Value" DisplayName="SubjectId" Description="The subject: the mouse's lab ID, or test." />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="StringProperty">
                <Value></Value>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Take">
                <rx:Count>1</rx:Count>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:AsyncSubject">
              <Name>SubjectId</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
              <Property Name="SessionId" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="PropertyMapping">
              <PropertyMappings>
                <Property Name="SubjectId" />
              </PropertyMappings>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>SubjectId</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Control:ExperimentControl.bonsai">
              <SubjectId>UNMAPPED</SubjectId>
              <SessionId />
              <ControlEndpoint>@tcp://127.0.0.1:5561</ControlEndpoint>
              <Parameters>
                <Parameter>
                  <Name>TrainingStage</Name>
                  <Value>4</Value>
                  <Description>Row of the task file's trainingStages to run: the GUI's Training Stage. A row past the end of the task file's table stops the workflow at Go.</Description>
                  <Minimum>0</Minimum>
                  <Maximum>4</Maximum>
                  <WholeNumber>true</WholeNumber>
                </Parameter>
                <Parameter>
                  <Name>SpoutStepSize</Name>
                  <Value />
                  <Description>Motor steps each spout nudge moves, taken live (HarpLickSpoutStage's StepSize).</Description>
                  <Minimum>1</Minimum>
                  <WholeNumber>true</WholeNumber>
                </Parameter>
              </Parameters>
              <Commands>
                <Command>
                  <Name>RewardLeft</Name>
                  <Description>Deliver ManualRewardDropUl (2.5 ul) on the left spout.</Description>
                </Command>
                <Command>
                  <Name>RewardRight</Name>
                  <Description>Deliver ManualRewardDropUl (2.5 ul) on the right spout.</Description>
                </Command>
                <Command>
                  <Name>SpoutsHome</Name>
                  <Description>Move both spouts to the home position.</Description>
                </Command>
                <Command>
                  <Name>SpoutsIn</Name>
                  <Description>Move both spouts to the in position.</Description>
                </Command>
                <Command>
                  <Name>SpoutsOut</Name>
                  <Description>Move both spouts to the out position.</Description>
                </Command>
                <Command>
                  <Name>SaveSpoutPositions</Name>
                  <Description>Save the spouts' in positions to this mouse's file.</Description>
                </Command>
                <Command>
                  <Name>LeftUp</Name>
                  <Description>Nudge the left spout up by SpoutStepSize.</Description>
                </Command>
                <Command>
                  <Name>LeftDown</Name>
                  <Description>Nudge the left spout down by SpoutStepSize.</Description>
                </Command>
                <Command>
                  <Name>RightUp</Name>
                  <Description>Nudge the right spout up by SpoutStepSize.</Description>
                </Command>
                <Command>
                  <Name>RightDown</Name>
                  <Description>Nudge the right spout down by SpoutStepSize.</Description>
                </Command>
                <Command>
                  <Name>LeftFront</Name>
                  <Description>Nudge the left spout forward by SpoutStepSize.</Description>
                </Command>
                <Command>
                  <Name>LeftBack</Name>
                  <Description>Nudge the left spout back by SpoutStepSize.</Description>
                </Command>
                <Command>
                  <Name>RightFront</Name>
                  <Description>Nudge the right spout forward by SpoutStepSize.</Description>
                </Command>
                <Command>
                  <Name>RightBack</Name>
                  <Description>Nudge the right spout back by SpoutStepSize.</Description>
                </Command>
                <Command>
                  <Name>BaseLeft</Name>
                  <Description>Nudge the spout base left by SpoutStepSize.</Description>
                </Command>
                <Command>
                  <Name>BaseRight</Name>
                  <Description>Nudge the spout base right by SpoutStepSize.</Description>
                </Command>
              </Commands>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>SubjectId</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>ExperimentGo</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>SessionId</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>ExperimentGo</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:ParameterValue">
                <orcl:Name>TrainingStage</orcl:Name>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>ExperimentGo</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
              <scr:Name>StageToInt</scr:Name>
              <scr:Expression>Convert.ToInt32(it)</scr:Expression>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Zip" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Take">
                <rx:Count>1</rx:Count>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:Condition">
              <Name>RunSettingsValid</Name>
              <Description>Subject and session given.</Description>
              <Workflow>
                <Nodes>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowInput">
                    <Name>Source1</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
                    <scr:Expression>Item1.Trim().Length &gt; 0 &amp;&amp; Item2.Trim().Length &gt; 0</scr:Expression>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowOutput" />
                </Nodes>
                <Edges>
                  <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
                </Edges>
              </Workflow>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:First" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:AsyncSubject">
              <Name>RunSettings</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>RunSettings</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>Item3</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:AsyncSubject">
              <Name>TrainingStage</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="StringProperty">
                <Value>..\config\task-localization.yml</Value>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Take">
                <rx:Count>1</rx:Count>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:AsyncSubject">
              <Name>TaskFilePath</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
              <Property Name="Value" DisplayName="TaskPath" Description="The task file: rig-control's copy of the one chosen at launch, read at Start for the background noise and again at Go with the form's edits; from the editor, config\task-localization.yml." />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="IntProperty">
                <Value>150</Value>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:BehaviorSubject">
              <Name>SpoutStepSize</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>ControlEvents</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:OnParameterSet">
                <orcl:Name>SpoutStepSize</orcl:Name>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
              <scr:Name>StepSizeToInt</scr:Name>
              <scr:Expression>Convert.ToInt32(it)</scr:Expression>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
              <Name>SpoutStepSize</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="DoubleProperty">
                <Value>2.5</Value>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:BehaviorSubject">
              <Name>ManualRewardDropUl</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>SpoutStepSize</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Take">
                <rx:Count>1</rx:Count>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:DelaySubscription">
                <rx:DueTime>PT1S</rx:DueTime>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:ParameterDefault">
                <orcl:Name>SpoutStepSize</orcl:Name>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="2" To="3" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="6" To="5" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="4" To="7" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="5" To="7" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="9" To="8" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="11" To="10" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="13" To="12" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="12" To="14" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="8" To="15" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="10" To="15" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="14" To="15" Label="Source3" />
            <Edge From="15" To="16" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="16" To="17" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="17" To="18" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="18" To="19" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="20" To="21" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="21" To="22" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="23" To="24" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="24" To="25" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="26" To="23" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="27" To="28" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="29" To="30" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="30" To="31" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="31" To="32" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="33" To="34" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="35" To="36" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="36" To="37" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="37" To="38" Label="Source1" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
        <Name>TaskFile</Name>
        <Description>Reads the task file (TaskPath) at Start into LaunchTaskConfig, as rig-control wrote it at launch, for the background noise, which plays from Ready; and at Go, with the form's edits, into TaskConfig. Go stops the workflow if backgroundNoise was changed after launch, as the noise already plays at the launch's level.</Description>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>ExperimentGo</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Take">
                <rx:Count>1</rx:Count>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>TaskFilePath</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Zip" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>Item2</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="core:ReadTextFile" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="p6:DeserializeFromYaml">
              <p6:Type xsi:type="TypeMapping" TypeArguments="p6:UclOpenCoenDomeDecisionMakingTaskLogic" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:AsyncSubject">
              <Name>TaskConfig</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>TaskFilePath</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="core:ReadTextFile" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="p6:DeserializeFromYaml">
              <p6:Type xsi:type="TypeMapping" TypeArguments="p6:UclOpenCoenDomeDecisionMakingTaskLogic" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:AsyncSubject">
              <Name>LaunchTaskConfig</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>TaskConfig</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>LaunchTaskConfig</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Zip" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:Condition">
              <Name>BackgroundNoiseChanged?</Name>
              <Workflow>
                <Nodes>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowInput">
                    <Name>Source1</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
                    <scr:Expression>Item1.TaskParameters.BackgroundNoise.Enabled != Item2.TaskParameters.BackgroundNoise.Enabled || Item1.TaskParameters.BackgroundNoise.LevelDbfs != Item2.TaskParameters.BackgroundNoise.LevelDbfs</scr:Expression>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowOutput" />
                </Nodes>
                <Edges>
                  <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
                </Edges>
              </Workflow>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="StringProperty">
                <Value>The background noise plays from Ready at the task file's backgroundNoise as launched, so it cannot be changed before Go: launch again to play it at another level.</Value>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="core:ThrowError" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>TaskConfig</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>TaskParameters.Optogenetics.UseZapit</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:AsyncSubject">
              <Name>Optogenetics</Name>
              <Description>Whether this is an optogenetics experiment, from the task file (TaskParameters.Optogenetics.UseZapit): ExperimentManifest requires Zapit&apos;s logs only while it is true (ExpectedFiles ?Optogenetics).</Description>
            </Expression>
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="1" To="3" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="2" To="3" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="3" To="4" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="4" To="5" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="5" To="6" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="6" To="7" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="8" To="9" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="9" To="10" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="10" To="11" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="12" To="14" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="13" To="14" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="14" To="15" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="15" To="16" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="16" To="17" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="18" To="19" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="19" To="20" Label="Source1" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
        <Name>Declarations</Name>
        <Description>Subjects the groups share. Trial (each trial as drawn) and TrialRow (each trial's BonsaiData_Trial row, built when the outcome is known); TrialEnds closes the trial loop; DecisionVariable and the grating's azimuth carry the response; VisualStimulus, VisualStimulusOff, AuditoryStimulus and PenaltySound start the stimuli; Zapit's commands and replies; RewardRequests, each (side, microlitres) reward, the side as rig.yml's wiring names it (left, right). Every subject a per-trial graph multicasts into is a BehaviorSubject: Bonsai passes a multicast's completion to a PublishSubject, so the first trial's graph closed it and the grating, the sound and the spouts ran on trial 1 only (BLUE-OPTO-2, 14 Nov 2026). VisualStimulusOff (subscribed per grating) and the blocks' LickSpoutStage.Commands and BehaviorBoard-Main.Commands are fed through VisualStimulusOffFeed, LickSpoutStageFeed and BehaviorBoardFeed, each relayed once at TaskLogic's top level.</Description>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:BehaviorSubject" TypeArguments="p1:Trial">
              <rx:Name>Trial</rx:Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:PublishSubject" TypeArguments="p1:TrialEnd">
              <rx:Name>TrialEnds</rx:Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:BehaviorSubject" TypeArguments="harp:Timestamped(p1:TrialRow)">
              <rx:Name>TrialRow</rx:Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:BehaviorSubject" TypeArguments="sys:Int32">
              <rx:Name>DecisionVariable</rx:Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:BehaviorSubject" TypeArguments="sys:Double">
              <rx:Name>GratingAzimuthStart</rx:Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:BehaviorSubject" TypeArguments="sys:Double">
              <rx:Name>GratingAzimuthDeg</rx:Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:BehaviorSubject" TypeArguments="p1:Trial">
              <rx:Name>VisualStimulus</rx:Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:PublishSubject" TypeArguments="harp:Timestamped(sys:Double)">
              <rx:Name>VisualStimulusOff</rx:Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:BehaviorSubject" TypeArguments="p1:Trial">
              <rx:Name>AuditoryStimulus</rx:Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:BehaviorSubject" TypeArguments="sys:String">
              <rx:Name>PenaltySound</rx:Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:PublishSubject" TypeArguments="zap:ZapitReply">
              <rx:Name>ZapitReplies</rx:Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:BehaviorSubject" TypeArguments="sys:Tuple(sys:String,sys:Double)">
              <rx:Name>RewardRequests</rx:Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:BehaviorSubject" TypeArguments="harp:Timestamped(sys:Double)">
              <rx:Name>VisualStimulusOffFeed</rx:Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:BehaviorSubject" TypeArguments="dev:LickSpoutCommand">
              <rx:Name>LickSpoutStageFeed</rx:Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:BehaviorSubject" TypeArguments="harp:HarpMessage">
              <rx:Name>BehaviorBoardFeed</rx:Name>
            </Expression>
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
        <Name>Hardware</Name>
        <Description>The dome's devices (OpenRigs.Devices RigHardware: boards, timestamp generator, lick spout stage, Lickety Splits, three cameras and their trigger, started 2 s after Start), which reports Ready once the spouts are homed, the Harp clock is set and the mixer has started (ReadyStages), and stops the workflow, naming what never came, if that takes longer than 180 s.</Description>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="PropertyMapping">
              <PropertyMappings>
                <Property Name="SpoutStepSize" />
              </PropertyMappings>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>SpoutStepSize</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Devices:RigHardware.bonsai">
              <ReadyWaitsFor>HarpClockSet, SpoutsHomed, MixerStarted</ReadyWaitsFor>
            </Expression>
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="1" To="0" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="0" To="2" Label="Source1" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
        <Property Name="DisplayDevice" Description="The display the dome projector is on; a launch property." />
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
        <Name>Display</Name>
        <Description>The dome projection (OpenRigs.Vision ProjectorDisplay, from rig.yml's projectionCalibration; DisplayDevice a launch property) and each trial's grating.</Description>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>RigConfigs</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>ProjectionCalibration</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Vision:ProjectorDisplay.bonsai">
              <DisplayDevice>First</DisplayDevice>
              <WindowState>Fullscreen</WindowState>
              <Width>1920</Width>
              <Height>1080</Height>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
              <Property Name="DisplayDevice" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>VisualStimulus</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:SelectMany">
              <Name>ShowGrating</Name>
              <Description>Draws a trial's grating from VisualStimulus until VisualStimulusOff: contrast, elevation and phase the trial's, the rest the task's, the azimuth GratingAzimuthDeg (closed loop moves it), flickering at the stimulus set's pulse rate, with the photodiode square black on its on frames and white on its off frames.</Description>
              <Workflow>
                <Nodes>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowInput">
                    <Name>Source1</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Take">
                      <rx:Count>1</rx:Count>
                    </Combinator>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="rx:AsyncSubject">
                    <Name>GratingTrial</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>DrawStimuli</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Name>Flicker</Name>
                    <Description>The grating on and off at the auditory stimulus set's pulse rate (AuditoryStimulusSet.PulseRateHz): each half period is its FlickerHalfPeriod, mapped in. A render-clock stimulus, not a task wait.</Description>
                    <Combinator xsi:type="gl:Timer">
                      <gl:DueTime>PT0S</gl:DueTime>
                      <gl:Period>PT0S</gl:Period>
                    </Combinator>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Mod">
                    <Operand xsi:type="WorkflowProperty" TypeArguments="sys:Int64">
                      <Value>2</Value>
                    </Operand>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="rx:WithLatestFrom" />
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="rx:Condition">
                    <Name>On?</Name>
                    <Workflow>
                      <Nodes>
                        <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowInput">
                          <Name>Source1</Name>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
                          <scr:Expression>Item2 == 0</scr:Expression>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowOutput" />
                      </Nodes>
                      <Edges>
                        <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
                      </Edges>
                    </Workflow>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
                    <Selector>Item1</Selector>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="rx:Condition">
                    <Name>Off?</Name>
                    <Workflow>
                      <Nodes>
                        <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowInput">
                          <Name>Source1</Name>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
                          <scr:Expression>Item2 != 0</scr:Expression>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowOutput" />
                      </Nodes>
                      <Edges>
                        <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
                      </Edges>
                    </Workflow>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
                    <Selector>Item1</Selector>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="PropertyMapping">
                    <PropertyMappings>
                      <Property Name="Contrast" Selector="visualContrast" />
                      <Property Name="LocationY" Selector="visualElevationDeg" />
                      <Property Name="Phase" Selector="visualPhaseRad" />
                    </PropertyMappings>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>GratingTrial</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="PropertyMapping">
                    <PropertyMappings>
                      <Property Name="TemporalFrequency" Selector="TaskParameters.VisualStimulus.TemporalFrequencyHz" />
                      <Property Name="SpatialFrequency" Selector="TaskParameters.VisualStimulus.SpatialFrequencyCpd" />
                      <Property Name="Angle" Selector="TaskParameters.VisualStimulus.OrientationDeg" />
                    </PropertyMappings>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>TaskConfig</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="PropertyMapping">
                    <PropertyMappings>
                      <Property Name="Aperture" Selector="it" />
                    </PropertyMappings>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
                    <scr:Name>Aperture</scr:Name>
                    <scr:Description>The Gaussian window's sigma relative to the grating's 100 degree extent.</scr:Description>
                    <scr:Expression>TaskParameters.VisualStimulus.GaussianWindowSigmaDeg * 2 / 100.0</scr:Expression>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="PropertyMapping">
                    <PropertyMappings>
                      <Property Name="LocationX" />
                    </PropertyMappings>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>GratingAzimuthDeg</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="BonVision:Primitives.DrawGratings.bonsai">
                    <LocationX>0</LocationX>
                    <LocationY>0</LocationY>
                    <Layer>0</Layer>
                    <ExtentX>100</ExtentX>
                    <ExtentY>100</ExtentY>
                    <SpatialFrequency>0.06666667</SpatialFrequency>
                    <TemporalFrequency>0</TemporalFrequency>
                    <Phase>0</Phase>
                    <Angle>0</Angle>
                    <SquareWave>false</SquareWave>
                    <Contrast>0</Contrast>
                    <DutyCycle xsi:nil="true" />
                    <Radius>1</Radius>
                    <Aperture>0.4</Aperture>
                    <Opacity>1</Opacity>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>VisualStimulusOff</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="rx:TakeUntil" />
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowOutput" />
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="rx:TakeUntil" />
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="BonVision:Primitives.DrawQuad.bonsai">
                    <ExtentX>30</ExtentX>
                    <ExtentY>30</ExtentY>
                    <LocationX>130</LocationX>
                    <LocationY>-22.5</LocationY>
                    <Layer>0</Layer>
                    <Angle>0</Angle>
                    <ColorR>0</ColorR>
                    <ColorG>0</ColorG>
                    <ColorB>0</ColorB>
                    <ColorA>1</ColorA>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="rx:TakeUntil" />
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="BonVision:Primitives.DrawQuad.bonsai">
                    <ExtentX>30</ExtentX>
                    <ExtentY>30</ExtentY>
                    <LocationX>130</LocationX>
                    <LocationY>-22.5</LocationY>
                    <Layer>0</Layer>
                    <Angle>0</Angle>
                    <ColorR>1</ColorR>
                    <ColorG>1</ColorG>
                    <ColorB>1</ColorB>
                    <ColorA>1</ColorA>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="rx:IgnoreElements" />
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>AuditoryStimulusSet</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="PropertyMapping">
                    <PropertyMappings>
                      <Property Name="Period" Selector="FlickerHalfPeriod" />
                    </PropertyMappings>
                  </Expression>
                </Nodes>
                <Edges>
                  <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="4" To="5" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="3" To="6" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="5" To="6" Label="Source2" />
                  <Edge From="6" To="7" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="7" To="8" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="6" To="9" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="9" To="10" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="12" To="11" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="14" To="13" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="14" To="16" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="16" To="15" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="18" To="17" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="8" To="19" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="11" To="19" Label="Source2" />
                  <Edge From="13" To="19" Label="Source3" />
                  <Edge From="15" To="19" Label="Source4" />
                  <Edge From="17" To="19" Label="Source5" />
                  <Edge From="19" To="21" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="20" To="21" Label="Source2" />
                  <Edge From="21" To="22" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="8" To="24" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="24" To="23" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="20" To="23" Label="Source2" />
                  <Edge From="10" To="26" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="26" To="25" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="20" To="25" Label="Source2" />
                  <Edge From="2" To="27" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="28" To="29" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="29" To="4" Label="Source1" />
                </Edges>
              </Workflow>
            </Expression>
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="3" To="2" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="4" To="5" Label="Source1" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
        <Name>Audio</Name>
        <Description>The speakers and their mixer (OpenRigs.Audio SpeakerMixer: Speakers, and the mixer started no sooner than 3 s after Start, never sooner, as a fault while the sound card boots can blue-screen the PC); each trial's sound and the penalty sound at the task file's level in dBFS RMS (levelDbfs), checked when the task file is read at Go; the background noise at the launch's task file's level, checked at Start and sent at Ready.</Description>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Audio:SpeakerMixer.bonsai" />
            <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
              <Name>LoadAudioFiles</Name>
              <Description>The auditory stimulus set equalised for rig.yml's speakers at Start (LoadAuditoryStimulusSet), then at Go at the task's audioStimulus.levelDbfs (LevelAuditoryStimulusSet, which stops the workflow if any would peak at -1 dBFS after equalisation); the lab's penalty sound on penaltySoundChannel at penalty.sound.levelDbfs; the background noise, checked to be at the mixer's rate, on every speaker unequalised at the launch's task file's backgroundNoise.levelDbfs (LaunchTaskConfig), laid out at Start and sent to the mixer at Ready, which fades it in over 2 s.</Description>
              <Workflow>
                <Nodes>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>Speakers</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="p1:LoadAuditoryStimulusSet">
                      <p1:Folder>LocalFiles\AuditoryStimuli</p1:Folder>
                      <p1:FilePrefix>filtered_pink_pulse_train_</p1:FilePrefix>
                    </Combinator>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Take">
                      <rx:Count>1</rx:Count>
                    </Combinator>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="rx:AsyncSubject">
                    <Name>AuditoryStimulusSet</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>AuditoryStimulusSet</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>TaskConfig</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
                    <Selector>TaskParameters.AudioStimulus.LevelDbfs</Selector>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Zip" />
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="p1:LevelAuditoryStimulusSet" />
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="rx:AsyncSubject">
                    <Name>LevelledStimulusSet</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>TaskConfig</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
                    <Selector>TaskParameters.Penalty.Sound.LevelDbfs</Selector>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>Speakers</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Zip" />
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="InputMapping">
                    <PropertyMappings>
                      <Property Name="LevelDbfs" Selector="Item1" />
                    </PropertyMappings>
                    <Selector>Item2</Selector>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="aud:PenaltySoundBuffer">
                      <aud:LevelDbfs>-30</aud:LevelDbfs>
                    </Combinator>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Take">
                      <rx:Count>1</rx:Count>
                    </Combinator>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="rx:AsyncSubject">
                    <Name>PenaltySoundBuffer</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="al:AudioReader">
                      <al:FileName>LocalFiles\background_white_noise.wav</al:FileName>
                      <al:BufferLength>0</al:BufferLength>
                      <al:SampleRate>0</al:SampleRate>
                    </Combinator>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Take">
                      <rx:Count>1</rx:Count>
                    </Combinator>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="rx:AsyncSubject">
                    <Name>BackgroundNoiseWave</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>RigConfigs</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
                    <Selector>SpeakerArray.Device.SampleRate</Selector>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Name>BackgroundNoiseRate</Name>
                    <Description>The background noise must be at the mixer's rate (AudioReader keeps the file's): checked at Start.</Description>
                    <Combinator xsi:type="aud:CheckWaveRate">
                      <aud:FileName>LocalFiles\background_white_noise.wav</aud:FileName>
                    </Combinator>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>LaunchTaskConfig</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="rx:Condition">
                    <Name>BackgroundNoiseEnabled?</Name>
                    <Workflow>
                      <Nodes>
                        <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowInput">
                          <Name>Source1</Name>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
                          <Selector>TaskParameters.BackgroundNoise.Enabled</Selector>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowOutput" />
                      </Nodes>
                      <Edges>
                        <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
                      </Edges>
                    </Workflow>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
                    <Selector>TaskParameters.BackgroundNoise.LevelDbfs</Selector>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>Speakers</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>BackgroundNoiseWave</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Zip" />
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Zip" />
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="InputMapping">
                    <PropertyMappings>
                      <Property Name="LevelDbfs" Selector="Item1" />
                    </PropertyMappings>
                    <Selector>Item2</Selector>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="aud:SpeakerBuffer">
                      <aud:Channels />
                      <aud:LevelDbfs>-50</aud:LevelDbfs>
                      <aud:Equalise>false</aud:Equalise>
                      <aud:SyncCopy>false</aud:SyncCopy>
                    </Combinator>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
                    <Name>BackgroundNoise</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
                    <Name>Ready</Name>
                    <Description>Passes on once every stage RigHardware's ReadyWaitsFor names has come, the moment RigHardware reports Ready: HarpClockSet, the spouts homed (LickSpoutStage.Homed) and the mixer started (MixerStarted, SpeakerMixer's one stage on ReadyStages), so the background noise starts at Ready.</Description>
                    <Workflow>
                      <Nodes>
                        <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                          <Name>HarpClockSet</Name>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                          <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Take">
                            <rx:Count>1</rx:Count>
                          </Combinator>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                          <Name>LickSpoutStage.Homed</Name>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                          <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Take">
                            <rx:Count>1</rx:Count>
                          </Combinator>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                          <Name>ReadyStages</Name>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                          <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Take">
                            <rx:Count>1</rx:Count>
                          </Combinator>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                          <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Zip" />
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowOutput" />
                      </Nodes>
                      <Edges>
                        <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="2" To="3" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="4" To="5" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="1" To="6" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="3" To="6" Label="Source2" />
                        <Edge From="5" To="6" Label="Source3" />
                        <Edge From="6" To="7" Label="Source1" />
                      </Edges>
                    </Workflow>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Zip" />
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
                    <Selector>Item1</Selector>
                  </Expression>
                </Nodes>
                <Edges>
                  <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="2" To="3" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="4" To="7" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="5" To="6" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="6" To="7" Label="Source2" />
                  <Edge From="7" To="8" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="8" To="9" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="10" To="11" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="11" To="13" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="12" To="13" Label="Source2" />
                  <Edge From="13" To="14" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="14" To="15" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="15" To="16" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="16" To="17" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="18" To="19" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="19" To="20" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="21" To="22" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="22" To="23" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="24" To="25" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="25" To="26" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="27" To="29" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="28" To="29" Label="Source2" />
                  <Edge From="26" To="30" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="29" To="30" Label="Source2" />
                  <Edge From="30" To="31" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="31" To="32" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="32" To="35" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="34" To="35" Label="Source2" />
                  <Edge From="35" To="36" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="36" To="33" Label="Source1" />
                </Edges>
              </Workflow>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>AuditoryStimulus</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:Condition">
              <Name>AudioEnabled?</Name>
              <Description>Discrimination's visual and neutral trials play no sound.</Description>
              <Workflow>
                <Nodes>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowInput">
                    <Name>Source1</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
                    <scr:Expression>audioEnabled</scr:Expression>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowOutput" />
                </Nodes>
                <Edges>
                  <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
                </Edges>
              </Workflow>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:SelectMany">
              <Name>PlayStim</Name>
              <Description>Plays a trial's sound: its waveform equalised for its speaker (the channel of rig.yml's speaker nearest the drawn location), at the task's audioStimulus.levelDbfs, with the sync copy on rig.yml's syncChannel at syncGain.</Description>
              <Workflow>
                <Nodes>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowInput">
                    <Name>Source1</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Take">
                      <rx:Count>1</rx:Count>
                    </Combinator>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="rx:AsyncSubject">
                    <Name>SoundTrial</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Zip" />
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>LevelledStimulusSet</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>SoundTrial</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="p1:SelectAuditoryStimulus" />
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
                    <Name>StimulusSounds</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="rx:IgnoreElements" />
                  </Expression>
                </Nodes>
                <Edges>
                  <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="4" To="3" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="5" To="3" Label="Source2" />
                  <Edge From="3" To="6" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="2" To="8" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="6" To="7" Label="Source1" />
                </Edges>
              </Workflow>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>PenaltySound</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:SelectMany">
              <Name>PlayPenaltySound</Name>
              <Description>Plays the lab's penalty sound (OpenRigs.Audio PenaltySoundBuffer, made at Go): rig.yml's penaltySoundChannel alone, equalised for that speaker, at the task's penalty.sound.levelDbfs.</Description>
              <Workflow>
                <Nodes>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>PenaltySoundBuffer</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Take">
                      <rx:Count>1</rx:Count>
                    </Combinator>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
                    <Name>PenaltySounds</Name>
                  </Expression>
                </Nodes>
                <Edges>
                  <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
                </Edges>
              </Workflow>
            </Expression>
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="2" To="3" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="3" To="4" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="5" To="6" Label="Source1" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
        <Name>Zapit</Name>
        <Description>Zapit, from Go and only when the task sets optogenetics.useZapit: OpenRigs.Devices Zapit.ConnectZapit, given the task's conditions file, connects to rig.yml's Zapit, carries ZapitCommands and ZapitReplies, and stops the workflow on an error reply, no conditions file loaded, a conditions count other than the file's, or a real mouse on a rig without hardware triggering.</Description>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>TaskConfig</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Take">
                <rx:Count>1</rx:Count>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:Condition">
              <Name>OptogeneticsExperiment?</Name>
              <Workflow>
                <Nodes>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowInput">
                    <Name>Source1</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
                    <Selector>TaskParameters.Optogenetics.UseZapit</Selector>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowOutput" />
                </Nodes>
                <Edges>
                  <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
                </Edges>
              </Workflow>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>TaskParameters.Optogenetics.ZapitConfigPath</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Devices:Zapit.ConnectZapit.bonsai" />
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="2" To="3" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="3" To="4" Label="Source1" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
        <Name>Logging</Name>
        <Description>Everything written to the experiment folder: LogControllerLogic makes it at Go and publishes PathPrefix; BonsaiData_Async (LogAsync) takes the controller's events and each reward from Start; HarpLogs logs every Harp device once the folder exists and the Harp clock is set; DeliverReward (OpenRigs.Devices) plans each (side, microlitres) reward on the valve's calibration, fires it on the Harp clock and logs it as RewardDelivered with each calibration as ValveCalibrationDO&lt;n&gt; (a valve with no calibration stops the workflow, for every mouse); ExperimentLogs holds the rest; RecordHarpDevices and ExperimentManifest record the devices and the experiment.</Description>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
              <Name>LogControllerLogic</Name>
              <Description>Waits for Go (RunSettings: the controller's SubjectId and SessionId), then LogController creates the experiment folder RootPath\sub-&lt;SubjectId&gt;\ses-&lt;SessionId&gt;_&lt;DateTime&gt; and publishes it as PathPrefix, which every log waits for. RootPath is rig.yml's, the rig's acquisition folder itself (C:\Coen-Lab-Local\Acquired-Data): experiments have no project folder.</Description>
              <Workflow>
                <Nodes>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>RunSettings</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="PropertyMapping">
                    <PropertyMappings>
                      <Property Name="SubjectId" Selector="Item1" />
                      <Property Name="SessionId" Selector="Item2" />
                    </PropertyMappings>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>RigConfigs</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
                    <Selector>RootPath</Selector>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="PropertyMapping">
                    <PropertyMappings>
                      <Property Name="Path" />
                    </PropertyMappings>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Logging:LogController.bonsai">
                    <SubjectId>UNMAPPED</SubjectId>
                    <SessionId>UNMAPPED</SessionId>
                    <Path>C:\Coen-Lab-Local\Acquired-Data</Path>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="rx:DelaySubscription">
                      <rx:DueTime>PT1S</rx:DueTime>
                    </Combinator>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>RunSettings</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="rx:SubscribeWhen" />
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowOutput" />
                </Nodes>
                <Edges>
                  <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="2" To="3" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="3" To="4" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="1" To="5" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="4" To="5" Label="Source2" />
                  <Edge From="5" To="6" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="6" To="8" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="7" To="8" Label="Source2" />
                  <Edge From="8" To="9" Label="Source1" />
                </Edges>
              </Workflow>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Logging:LogAsync.bonsai" />
            <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Devices:HarpLogs.bonsai" />
            <Expression xsi:type="PropertyMapping">
              <PropertyMappings>
                <Property Name="RigFile" />
              </PropertyMappings>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>RigFile</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Devices:BehaviorBoard.DeliverReward.bonsai">
              <RigFile>UNMAPPED</RigFile>
              <CalibrationDirectory />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>RewardRequests</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>PathPrefix</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:SelectMany">
              <Name>ExperimentLogs</Name>
              <Description>Every log that waits for the experiment folder (PathPrefix): BonsaiData_Trial (LogTrial of TrialRow), the cameras (OpenRigs.Logging LogCameras), the settings files and Zapit's logs (OpenRigs.Devices Zapit.ZapitLogs: its replies and Settings_ZapitConditions). The RngSeed event is TaskLogic's, at trial 1's Go.</Description>
              <Workflow>
                <Nodes>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>TrialRow</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Logging:LogTrial.bonsai" />
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>RigConfigs</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="p2:SerializeToJson">
                      <p2:Formatting>Indented</p2:Formatting>
                    </Combinator>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Logging:LogDataSchema.bonsai">
                    <Name>Settings_Rig</Name>
                    <Extension>json</Extension>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>TaskConfig</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="p6:SerializeToJson">
                      <p6:Formatting>Indented</p6:Formatting>
                    </Combinator>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Logging:LogDataSchema.bonsai">
                    <Name>Settings_Task</Name>
                    <Extension>json</Extension>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>ExperimentGo</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:ExperimentSettings" />
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Logging:LogDataSchema.bonsai">
                    <Name>Settings_Experiment</Name>
                    <Extension>json</Extension>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Logging:LogCameras.bonsai" />
                  <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Devices:Zapit.ZapitLogs.bonsai" />
                </Nodes>
                <Edges>
                  <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="2" To="3" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="3" To="4" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="5" To="6" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="6" To="7" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="8" To="9" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="9" To="10" Label="Source1" />
                </Edges>
              </Workflow>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>PathPrefix</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:ReportMetric">
                <orcl:Name>path</orcl:Name>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:ReportPhase">
                <orcl:Phase>Recording</orcl:Phase>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="hd:RecordHarpDevices">
              <Name>RecordHarpDevices</Name>
              <Description>Checks every Harp device in rig.yml at Start and records it into each experiment (OpenRigs.HarpDevices): the Behavior board, the timestamp generator, both stepper drivers and both Lickety Splits (each a rig.yml entry with a portName whose data the workflow publishes as &lt;Name&gt;.Data) must be on their portName with their usbSerial, or the workflow stops saying which board is where; 0.5 s after the experiment folder appears it asks each for a register dump on &lt;Name&gt;.Commands, which its log records; and it writes &lt;Name&gt;\&lt;Name&gt;_device.json and the register map &lt;Name&gt;\&lt;Name&gt;.yml, which ExperimentManifest expects (harp).</Description>
              <hd:ConfigRoot>C:\Coen-Lab-Local\RigConfigs</hd:ConfigRoot>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="mf:ExperimentManifest">
              <Name>ExperimentManifest</Name>
              <Description>Writes manifest.json into the experiment folder (OpenRigs.Manifest), finding PathPrefix itself: once when the folder appears and again when the workflow stops. No run is connected: an experiment ends with the controller's Stop, recorded as stopped with its reason. It records the machine, this repo's commit, Bonsai's command line, who launched it and sent Go (every parameter at Go is in Settings_Experiment), rig.yml's path and hash and, each by its hash, the calibration files it and the workflow read by path (MeshMap.csv, gammalut.bmp, the speakers' filters; the auditory stimuli are this repo's, in src\LocalFiles\AuditoryStimuli, so the commit names them; each valve's calibration is in the experiment as ValveCalibrationDO&lt;n&gt;) and this mouse's spout positions (LickSpoutPositions\{SubjectId}.csv), what each BonsaiData_Trial column means (schemas\trial-columns.yml, copied in at Start), and what the experiment must leave: a folder for each device in rig.yml (BehaviorBoard-Main, TimestampGeneratorGen3-Main, StepperDriver-A/B, LicketySplit-Left/Right, Camera-Face/Pupil/Body), the record and register map RecordHarpDevices writes for each Harp device (harp), each of the three settings files in Settings (Settings/Settings_Rig_, Settings/Settings_Task_, Settings/Settings_Experiment_, each expected on its own) and BonsaiData (BonsaiData_Trial and BonsaiData_Async), which the overnight copy (jacuzzi-ingest's ingest-rig) alarms on if missing.</Description>
              <mf:IngestScript>coen-dome-decision-making</mf:IngestScript>
              <mf:ConfigFiles>C:\Coen-Lab-Local\RigConfigs\%COMPUTERNAME%\rig.yml;C:\Coen-Lab-Local\RigConfigs\%COMPUTERNAME%\calibration\MeshMap.csv;C:\Coen-Lab-Local\RigConfigs\%COMPUTERNAME%\calibration\gammalut.bmp;C:\Coen-Lab-Local\RigConfigs\%COMPUTERNAME%\calibration\speaker-left.json;C:\Coen-Lab-Local\RigConfigs\%COMPUTERNAME%\calibration\speaker-right.json;C:\Coen-Lab-Local\RigConfigs\%COMPUTERNAME%\calibration\speaker-centre.json;C:\Coen-Lab-Local\RigConfigs\%COMPUTERNAME%\calibration\LickSpoutPositions\{SubjectId}.csv</mf:ConfigFiles>
              <mf:ExpectedFiles>auto;harp;Settings/Settings_Rig_;Settings/Settings_Task_;Settings/Settings_Experiment_;BonsaiData/BonsaiData_Trial_;BonsaiData/BonsaiData_Async_;BonsaiData/BonsaiData_ZapitReplies_?Optogenetics;Settings/Settings_ZapitConditions_?Optogenetics</mf:ExpectedFiles>
              <mf:TrialColumns>schemas\trial-columns.yml</mf:TrialColumns>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>ControlEvents</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
              <scr:Expression>new((it.Kind.ToString() == &quot;Command&quot; ? it.Name : it.Kind.ToString()) as Event, it.ToString() as Detail)</scr:Expression>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="orl:CreateAsyncEvent">
                <orl:Event>Control</orl:Event>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="Bonsai.Harp:WithLatestTimestamp.bonsai">
              <Name>Timestamp</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
              <Name>AsyncEvents</Name>
            </Expression>
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="4" To="3" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="6" To="5" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="3" To="5" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="7" To="8" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="9" To="10" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="10" To="11" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="14" To="15" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="15" To="16" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="16" To="17" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="17" To="18" Label="Source1" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
        <Name>Status</Name>
        <Description>The current trial's facts as metrics, named as BonsaiData_Trial's columns (trialNumber, target, trialType, visualAzimuthDeg, audioAzimuthDeg, rewardSizeUl, laserCondition) and the trainingStage; rig-control computes counts, water and performance from the files.</Description>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>Trial</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>trialNumber</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:ReportMetric">
                <orcl:Name>trialNumber</orcl:Name>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>target</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:ReportMetric">
                <orcl:Name>target</orcl:Name>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>trialType</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:ReportMetric">
                <orcl:Name>trialType</orcl:Name>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>visualAzimuthDeg</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:ReportMetric">
                <orcl:Name>visualAzimuthDeg</orcl:Name>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>audioAzimuthDeg</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:ReportMetric">
                <orcl:Name>audioAzimuthDeg</orcl:Name>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>rewardSizeUl</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:ReportMetric">
                <orcl:Name>rewardSizeUl</orcl:Name>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>laserCondition</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:ReportMetric">
                <orcl:Name>laserCondition</orcl:Name>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>TrainingStage</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:ReportMetric">
                <orcl:Name>trainingStage</orcl:Name>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="0" To="3" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="3" To="4" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="0" To="5" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="5" To="6" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="0" To="7" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="7" To="8" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="0" To="9" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="9" To="10" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="0" To="11" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="11" To="12" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="0" To="13" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="13" To="14" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="15" To="16" Label="Source1" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
        <Name>Commands</Name>
        <Description>RewardLeft and RewardRight deliver ManualRewardDropUl (2.5 ul, Initialization) at that side (RewardRequests). The spout commands are HarpLickSpoutStage's own.</Description>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:WithLatestFrom" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>ControlEvents</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:OnCommand">
                <orcl:Name>RewardLeft</orcl:Name>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="StringProperty">
                <Value>left</Value>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>ManualRewardDropUl</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
              <Name>RewardRequests</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:WithLatestFrom" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>ControlEvents</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:OnCommand">
                <orcl:Name>RewardRight</orcl:Name>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="StringProperty">
                <Value>right</Value>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>ManualRewardDropUl</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
              <Name>RewardRequests</Name>
            </Expression>
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="2" To="3" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="3" To="0" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="4" To="0" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="0" To="5" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="7" To="8" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="8" To="9" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="9" To="6" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="10" To="6" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="6" To="11" Label="Source1" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
        <Name>TaskLogic</Name>
        <Description>The trial loop, every wait on the Harp clock (Core HarpDelay on Timestamp): the task checked at Go (CheckTaskAtGo); once the experiment folder exists, the spouts out (on a stage with spout movements) and the first trial drawn, its interval starting then. Each trial is drawn at the start of its interval (the last outcome, after any timeout); WaitForGo holds it until the interval's end less the lead (max(laserToStimulusSeconds, 0)) and the stage's quiet waits; the stimulus comes the lead after Go (LeadToStimulus) in every experiment; with optogenetics, Laser arms Zapit during the interval and raises the ZapitTrigger line at laserToStimulusSeconds before the stimulus (after it if negative), stopping the workflow if Zapit has not answered by then. Zapit adds no time.</Description>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>PathPrefix</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Take">
                <rx:Count>1</rx:Count>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Name>OnNextTick</Name>
              <Description>The experiment folder stamped with the next Harp clock tick and given from the clock's thread (OnNextTick, tested C#), so the first draw runs as every later one does. WithLatestTimestamp here ran it under a lock the clock needs, and the clock stopped at trial 1 (BLUE-OPTO-2, 14 Nov 2026).</Description>
              <Combinator xsi:type="p1:OnNextTick" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="p1:StartTrials" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Merge" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>TrialEnds</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>RigConfigs</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>SpeakerArray</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:CombineLatest" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>TaskConfig</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="PropertyMapping">
              <PropertyMappings>
                <Property Name="TrainingStage" />
              </PropertyMappings>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>TrainingStage</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Name>DrawTrial</Name>
              <Description>Draws each trial (TrialDraw, tested C#) at the start of its interval, from the last trial's end, the task and rig.yml's speakers; the first once the experiment folder exists, its interval starting then.</Description>
              <Combinator xsi:type="p1:DrawTrial">
                <p1:TrainingStage>0</p1:TrainingStage>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
              <Name>Trial</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>Timestamp</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>LickStateLeft</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>LickStateRight</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>WheelDistanceCm</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Name>WaitForGo</Name>
              <Description>Each trial's Go (tested C#), on the Harp clock: the end of its interval less the lead (max(laserToStimulusSeconds, 0)), or later until the stage's quiet waits both hold (both spouts released for lickQuietSeconds, a held contact blocking Go; the wheel within wheelQuietCm, forward and back added, over the last wheelQuietSeconds; each counted from the interval's start). Sets goTime and quietWaitSeconds.</Description>
              <Combinator xsi:type="p1:WaitForGo" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:BehaviorSubject">
              <Name>TrialGo</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="Bonsai.Harp:WithLatestTimestamp.bonsai">
              <Name>Timestamp</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="p1:SecondsUntil">
                <p1:Moment>Stimulus</p1:Moment>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="InputMapping">
              <PropertyMappings>
                <Property Name="DueSeconds" Selector="Item2" />
              </PropertyMappings>
              <Selector>Item1</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>Timestamp</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Name>LeadToStimulus</Name>
              <Description>The stimulus the lead (max(laserToStimulusSeconds, 0)) after Go, in every experiment, optogenetics on or off, so timing never reveals Zapit.</Description>
              <Combinator xsi:type="core:HarpDelay">
                <core:DueSeconds>0.0</core:DueSeconds>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:SelectMany">
              <Name>ExecuteTrial</Name>
              <Description>One trial on the Harp clock: the stimulus (VisualStimulus, AuditoryStimulus, its onset stamped as it is commanded; the grating off after stimulusSeconds), the spouts in after stimulusToSpoutsInSeconds, the response window after openLoopSeconds; at the outcome, the trial's row (TrialRow) and what the outcome sets off (TrialConsequence: the reward, the spouts, the penalty sound); then the timeout; at its end the TrialEnd leaves, stamped with the interval's start, so the next trial is drawn and Zapit armed while the interval runs; drinkSeconds into the interval the spouts go out, and the trial ends.</Description>
              <Workflow>
                <Nodes>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowInput">
                    <Name>Source1</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
                    <Selector>Value</Selector>
                  </Expression>
